{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/954408-invited-to-a-family-dinner","id":954408,"title":"Invited to a Family Dinner...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T08:37:02-07:00","id":954408,"title":"Invited to a Family Dinner...","content":"So, this come up as a pondering when thinking on a Beast with Family Ties, we know that the Beast can gain Satiety from a Family Dinner where they witness their chosen kin (if any) hunt and take down prey, whether for Vitae or what have you, the Beast can gain Satiety at the same time.<br /> <br /> What if a Beast has Family Ties with a Mage? Or a Promethean? Now, I haven't read Promethean 2nd yet, though these two splats aren't really hunter types... Prometheans can soak up Pyros though don't get it from living people like a Changeling could get Glamour from people even though they don't hunt... Mages power up with Mana and I suppose a Beast could join a particularly nebulous group of Mages in a hunt in the sticks ending in a blood sacrifice for that sweet tass though that's not the norm usually, right?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Mummies can collect Sekhem as I've rarely come across them and whilst my one friend does own the book, looking at it I found it pretty obtuse reading...<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the point of the post and thread here, how does your Beast solve a Family Dinner when their Kin doesn't hunt or in any other way feed off others? Or would you rule that for example's sake if your Beast and their Promethean bro went and got the latter some new Pyros that'd boost the Beast's Satiety even though no hunt or person was involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:13:52-07:00","id":954573,"title":"","content":"Hunt and Feeding are listed separately. I think any time a supernat replenishes their fuel stat that qualifies as a feeding, hunt is more limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:58:07-07:00","id":954760,"title":"","content":"Going to illustrate the corollary to Helms's point.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Family Dinner Systems</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to use Family Dinner, a Beast must accompany a supernatural being as he hunts, feeds, or both. It doesn\u2019t matter whether it\u2019s a vampire thirsting after blood, a werewolf stalking an intruder in his territory, or a changeling feeding on human emotions, so long as he is <b>actively tracking prey</b> and/or taking sustenance from a hunt. The Storyteller has the final say on whether or not an activity counts, but <b>it must involve a monster\u2019s supernatural nature or appetites directly</b>; mundane hunting or feeding does not invoke Family Dinner.<br /> <br /> <b>If the Beast witnesses a successful hunt \u2014 one that results in taking down the intended quarry, either literally or figuratively \u2014 she immediately regains 1 Satiety.</b> If she observes a successful feeding, she also gains 1 Satiety. These benefits are cumulative, so a hunt that also results in a feeding nets 2 Satiety total. The actual number of creatures involved in the scene does not matter. The Satiety gained is based on the acts witnessed, not the number of participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages pursuing their Obsessions to the detriment of other beings is thematically appropriate; ostensibly Tormented Prometheans regaining Willpower the only way the Condition allows them to operates similarly.<br /> <br /> On the more fuel-oriented side of things, there's a few example Legacy oblations that could conceivably serve the same function (to say nothing of Devouring the Slain), and the lacuna is still a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> The Arisen are more likely to let their cousins feed by performing the sorts of actions that earn them a reset on their Descent counter or cannibalizing relics.<br /> <br /> Speaking of cannibals, though, it's important to remember that Beasts are not confined to the PC splats when it comes to sympathetic consumption; Pandorans and Shuankhsen are valid kin, as are things from the Depths and the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:18:42-07:00","id":954798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/954408-invited-to-a-family-dinner?p=954760#post954760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of cannibals, though, it's important to remember that Beasts are not confined to the PC splats when it comes to sympathetic consumption; Pandorans and Shuankhsen are valid kin, as are things from the Depths and the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Beasts seem to emanate fear-resonant Essence do you think they establish some sort of recirculated feasting when among fear spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:04:31-07:00","id":954813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/954408-invited-to-a-family-dinner?p=954798#post954798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Beasts seem to emanate fear-resonant Essence do you think they establish some sort of recirculated feasting when among fear spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The nature of spirits in combination with the Begotten's lack of innate Twilight-sight makes this a bit tricky, but yes, ostensibly if you feed your Hunger in a fashion that allows phobophages to feed then you have a bit of a buffer.<br /> <br /> If your question is rather &quot;can a Beast get Satiety by letting fear-spirits consume the Essence they generate while in the Shadow,&quot; that's a little less definite due to the stipulations of needing the meal to be genuine predation; valid use would almost certainly involve the course of events wherein you've entered the Shadow and the fear-spirit is trying to eat you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:39:09-07:00","id":955093,"title":"","content":"I probably wouldn't allow a Beast to be creating fear essence unless they were using their powers such as Nightmares or what have you to actually generate fear in someone. It's a fair thing to spend satiety to sate it, though there'd also be the method of them travelling into the Shadow, also I'd find getting a bunch of fear spirits to chase my Beast like a swarm of hornets to sate the Horror a little... I dunno, counter-intuitive?<br /> <br /> One thing I hadn't considered was striking up kinship with a Goetic Demon. The Beast can use skeleton key to enter the Astral Space, though also I wonder just what sort of entrance they'd use to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:59:29-07:00","id":955159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/954408-invited-to-a-family-dinner?p=955093#post955093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably wouldn't allow a Beast to be creating fear essence unless they were using their powers such as Nightmares or what have you to actually generate fear in someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have the Resonant Condition relevant to their Family and Hunger while in the Shadow. Essence isn't supposed to be difficult to generate for spirits by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also I'd find getting a bunch of fear spirits to chase my Beast like a swarm of hornets to sate the Horror a little... I dunno, counter-intuitive? </div> </div> </div>The type of Begotten that grows the fastest through Kinship does so by being exploited by highly active mental-influence-having supernatural beings until they eventually cut ties with them through turnabout or retreat. Beasts thrive in dog-eat-dog environments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Beast can use skeleton key to enter the Astral Space, though also I wonder just what sort of entrance they'd use to do that? </div> </div> </div>There is no entrance they'd naturally use that facet of Kinship with; navigating to the rest of the Temenos is a function of Primordial Pathways or more conventional theme-hopping Astral travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:59:43-07:00","id":955330,"title":"","content":"Huh, rereading Primordial Pathways I never realised a Beast could just take one into Astral Space like that... That is actually... Kinda awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It could still fail and all if they've never ventured into the Astral before and there's no active Lair trait there, bad rolling or whatever... Though I really like a Beast can do that... I always just sorta figured the Pathways were used to summon the Lair into the physical world they were at and didn't realise the application of whilst being in the Lair using the Pathway to go somewhere else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}